 "capsule": "The Nogai Horde was a nomadic Turkic-Mongol confederation that emerged in the mid-15th century from the western wing of the dissolving Golden Horde, dominated by the descendants of the emir Edigu and centered on the steppe between the Volga and Ural rivers with its base at Saray-Jük. At its height it could field tens of thousands of horsemen and profited from trade routes linking Muscovy, the Crimean Khanate, and Central Asia. Devastated by famine, plague, and mounting Russian and Kazakh pressure in the 1550s, the horde split around 1557–1564 into the Great Nogai Horde and the Lesser (Small) Nogai Horde.",
